# CITATION.cff
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this case study, please cite it as below."
title: "Building a Transaction-Capable AI Agent Before There Was a Playbook"
abstract: >-
  An engineering case study of a production conversational agent that sold and
  provisioned eSIMs inside WhatsApp and Telegram, built and operated from July 2025
  to August 2026 on CPU-only infrastructure: architecture, security, evaluation,
  performance and economics, a catalogue of the failures it recorded, and the
  sources it draws on.
authors:
  - given-names: Joshua Peter
    family-names: Polaprayil
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoshPola96/enterprise-ai-agent-architecture-esim"
url: "https://github.com/JoshPola96/enterprise-ai-agent-architecture-esim"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agentic AI
  - LLM agents
  - conversational commerce
  - prompt injection
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - distributed systems
  - eSIM
